{
  "manufacturer": "ABB",
  "manufacturer_slug": "abb",
  "model": "ACH550-UH HVAC drive (embedded Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "ach550-uh",
  "short_model": "ACH550-UH",
  "aliases": [
    "ACH550-UH",
    "ACH550"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "ACH550-UH HVAC drives using the embedded fieldbus (EFB) RS-485 port on terminals X1:28-32 with 9802 = STD MODBUS; user's manual 3AUA0000081823 Rev F.",
  "summary": "ABB's ACH550-UH HVAC drive has an RS-485 port that can run Modbus RTU (or N2, FLN, BACnet). Control bits and relay outputs are coils, status bits and digital inputs are discrete inputs, and all parameters plus the control/status words and references are 16-bit holding registers, with parameter NNNN at register 4NNNN. This map covers the control block, main operating data, fault and alarm words, fault history and the EFB set-up parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual states the drive uses zero-based Modbus addressing: holding register 40002 is sent as 0001 and coil 33 as 0032. So 40001 = wire 0, parameter NNNN = register 4NNNN = wire NNNN - 1 (e.g. 0103 -> 40103 -> 102); coils 00001-00016 are control-word bits, 00033+ relay outputs; discrete inputs 10001-10032 are status-word bits and 10033+ digital inputs; input registers 30001/30002 are AI1/AI2."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ACH550-UH HVAC Drives User's Manual",
    "doc_number": "3AUA0000081823 Rev F",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://search.abb.com/library/Download.aspx?DocumentID=3AUA0000081823&LanguageCode=en&DocumentPartId=&Action=Launch",
    "pages": "Group 01 pp. 1-82 to 1-85; groups 03/04 pp. 1-86 to 1-91; 1607 p. 1-108; 3018/3019 p. 1-128; group 53 pp. 1-166 to 1-167; 9802 p. 1-184; EFB setup pp. 1-189 to 1-190; actual value scaling p. 1-199; Modbus protocol technical data pp. 1-239 to 1-246; ABB control profiles pp. 1-247 to 1-251 (printed page numbers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are 16-bit; there is no word order. Scaling uses each parameter's Resolution column, which the manual says multiplies the fieldbus integer (e.g. 0.1 Hz).",
    "40001/40004 work only with 5305 = ABB DRV LIM (default) or ABB DRV FULL; 40031-40034 only with the DCU profile. ABB DRV LIM ignores control word bits 4 and 10. The coil table labels ABB DRV LIM coil 00004 (bit 3) 'START' while the control-word table calls bit 3 INHIBIT OPERATION; it is the same bit.",
    "Discrete inputs 10001-10013 are listed with their ABB Drives profile meaning; with the DCU profile the same inputs carry DCU status bits (READY, ENABLED, STARTED, RUNNING...). Only 6 DI and 6 RO are listed; RO4-6 need the OREL-01 extension.",
    "Actual values 40005-40012 follow 5310-5317; 40005/40006 default to 0103 and 0104 according to the Modbus chapter, although the group 53 table lists 0 as the default of 5310-5317.",
    "Parity default is unclear: the group 53 list gives 5304 default 0 (8 NONE 1) while the EFB setup table appears to give 1 for Modbus. Read 5304 from the drive. 5303 baud (default 9.6 kbit/s) is left out because its fieldbus encoding is not stated.",
    "Left out: 0111 External ref 1 (Hz or rpm depending on 9904), PID, process-variable and energy-saving signals, fault time stamps 0402/0403, status/DI at fault, and the DCU REF registers 40045-40048, and input registers 30001/30002 (AI1/AI2 level 0-100 %, integer scaling not stated; use 0120/0121 instead).",
    "Exception 03 is returned for writes out of range, to read-only parameters, while started, or while a factory macro is selected."
  ],
